  "milestone": "core-structured-history-repair-source-v1",
  "predecessorCommit": "399cdc48765cad3482ef260addd6a8145c07ff60",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "scope": "Supply eight exact current and predecessor stop hashes in Rust, Python, .NET and Perl structured history tests. Require whole-source authentication before seven structured history readers reverse any edits: C, C++, Rust, Python, Ruby, .NET and JVM. Nine focused controls audit sixteen caller endpoints and authenticate eight unchanged Git-backed inventories, preserving unknown source bytes and rejecting forged transitions. Refresh exactly forty live source hashes across eleven files; preserve every other inventory byte. Original receipts, archives, runtime behavior, supported cells and installed acceptance claims do not change. Complete historical acceptance remains a hosted Core gate.",
